# VTID-03918 — commands run during this change

## Investigation

Read the full Web Speech API dictation lifecycle in
services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/app.js:
- operatorDictationSupported() / stopOperatorDictation() / startOperatorDictation()
- the mic button's onclick wiring (~line 26263-26284)
- every `if (state.chatDictationActive) stopOperatorDictation();` call site
  (sendChatMessage, backdrop close, X close)
- confirmed services/gateway/src/routes/command-hub.ts's CSP connect-src is
  not the cause: Chrome's Web Speech API network call is browser-process
  mediated, not a page-level fetch/XHR/WebSocket subject to page CSP, and
  no CSP header changed in this diff anyway.
- confirmed VTID-03910/VTID-03911 touched only styles.css — zero overlap
  with app.js's dictation code, ruling those changes out as the cause of
  this specific regression report.

Root cause: `recognition.start()` was called unguarded, with the active
state/class already applied beforehand — a synchronous throw (or any async
onerror code) left the mic button stuck red with no live recognition and
no visible explanation.

