## VALIDATOR-CHECK.yml's validate-pr job — missed on first push, caught by CI

The initial PR body used this repo's generic pull_request_template.md
layout, which has no `VALIDATION_PROFILE:` line — the workflow's
`validate-pr` job requires one (`grep -Eo 'VALIDATION_PROFILE:\s*[a-zA-Z0-9_/-]+'`
against the PR body) and rejects with exit 11 without it. Added
`VALIDATION_PROFILE: gateway_backend` to the top of the PR body via
`update_pull_request`. Note: re-running the SAME failed job
(`rerun_failed_jobs`) replays the ORIGINAL `pull_request` webhook payload
(including the stale PR body captured at push time) — it does NOT
re-fetch the current PR body, so the rerun still failed. A fresh commit
push (this one) triggers a new `synchronize` event that reads the PR body
live, which is what actually picks up the fix.

Second round, same class of gap: after VALIDATION_PROFILE was accepted,
the "Require PR markers" step (exit 12-15) rejected on the next gate,
missing SCOPE_ALLOWLIST/ACCEPTANCE/MERGE_PAYLOAD_PREVIEW/OASIS_IMPACT —
four more literal marker lines this repo's generic PR template doesn't
include. All four are presence-only `grep -q` checks (OASIS_IMPACT
additionally needs a yes|no value, checked later in the OASIS
Traceability Gate). Added all four to the PR body via update_pull_request,
then pushed this same commit to trigger the fresh synchronize event
needed to pick them up (same rerun-replays-stale-payload caveat as above).
